From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Artem Butusov <art.sormy@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 25 Oct 2026 16:30:00 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] clk: sunxi-ng: h616: Keep the TV encoder clock on its parent

Asked for 216 MHz, the TV encoder clock picked PLL-VIDEO0, which could
give it by changing rate; HDMI holds PLL-VIDEO0, the change is refused,
and the encoder is left at PLL-VIDEO0's rate halved. The encoder wants
PLL-VIDEO1, as Allwinner's driver sets it: keep the parent the device
tree assigns.

Signed-off-by: Artem Butusov <art.sormy@gmail.com>

---
diff --git a/drivers/clk/sunxi-ng/ccu-sun50i-h616.c b/drivers/clk/sunxi-ng/ccu-sun50i-h616.c
--- a/drivers/clk/sunxi-ng/ccu-sun50i-h616.c
+++ b/drivers/clk/sunxi-ng/ccu-sun50i-h616.c
@@ -687,7 +687,8 @@ static SUNXI_CCU_MP_WITH_MUX_GATE(tve0_clk, "tve0",
 				  8, 2,		/* P */
 				  24, 3,	/* mux */
 				  BIT(31),	/* gate */
-				  CLK_SET_RATE_PARENT);
+				  CLK_SET_RATE_PARENT |
+				  CLK_SET_RATE_NO_REPARENT);
 
 static SUNXI_CCU_GATE(bus_tve_top_clk, "bus-tve-top", "ahb3",
 		      0xb20, BIT(0), 0);
